  "title": "Wrongly and Apart: mis- and dis-",
  "short": "mis- means wrongly; dis- means apart, away or not.",
  "trouble": "Greek mis- or miso- means hate (misanthrope) and is a different part from the English mis- that means wrongly (mistake). dis- can mean not (dishonest), apart (dissect) or away (dismiss).",
  "prereqs": [
    "roots.not"
  ],
  "xp": 1,
