  "figureArchetype": "GeneralFigure",
  "lesson": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "Two prefixes that look alike do different jobs. <b>mis-</b> means “wrongly” or “badly”: a <i>mistake</i> is something taken wrongly, and to <i>misread</i> is to read wrongly. <b>dis-</b> means “apart,” “away” or “not”: to <i>dissect</i> is to cut apart, to <i>dismiss</i> is to send away and to <i>disagree</i> is to not agree."
      },
