      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "<b>mis-</b> = <b>wrongly, badly</b>. <b>dis-</b> = <b>apart, away, not</b>. Before <i>f</i>, <b>dis-</b> becomes <b>dif-</b> (<i>diffident</i>, <i>diffuse</i>)."
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "Many of the list’s <i>dis-</i> words use the “apart” sense. <b>Dissent</b> is feeling apart (<i>sent</i>, feel); <b>discord</b> is hearts apart (<i>cord</i>, heart); a <b>dissident</b> sits apart (<i>sid</i>, sit) from those in power. When you meet a new <i>dis-</i> word, try all three meanings and keep the one that fits."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "The parts and their words"
      },
