      {
        "t": "table",
        "head": [
          "Word and meaning",
          "Parts, and what they say"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "<b>mishap</b><br>an unlucky accident, usually minor",
            "<b>mis-</b> <i>badly</i> + hap <i>luck, chance</i><br>→ “bad luck”"
          ],
          [
            "<b><i>mistake</i></b><br>an error",
            "<b>mis-</b> <i>wrongly</i> + take<br>→ “take wrongly”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>dissent</b><br>disagreement with an official or common view",
            "<b>dis-</b> <i>apart</i> + sent <i>feel</i><br>→ “feeling apart”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>discord</b><br>disagreement; lack of harmony",
            "<b>dis-</b> <i>apart</i> + cord <i>heart</i><br>→ “hearts apart”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>diffident</b><br>shy and lacking confidence in oneself",
            "<b>dif-</b> <i>not</i> + fid <i>trust</i> + -ent<br>→ “not trusting (oneself)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>dissuade</b><br>to persuade not to do something",
            "<b>dis-</b> <i>away</i> + suad <i>urge</i><br>→ “urge away from”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>discern</b><br>to notice or tell apart, often with effort",
            "<b>dis-</b> <i>apart</i> + cern <i>sift, separate</i><br>→ “sift apart”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>dissident</b><br>a person who opposes official policy",
            "<b>dis-</b> <i>apart</i> + sid <i>sit</i> + -ent<br>→ “one who sits apart”"
          ]
        ],
        "cap": "Each word, what it means now, and its parts. Words in italics are familiar words that are not on the list."
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "Use the parts",
        "q": "Nothing her friends said could cheer her; she was <b>disconsolate</b>. What does the word mean?",
        "steps": [
          "Take it apart: <b>dis-</b> (not) + <b>consol</b> (comfort, as in <i>console</i>) + <b>-ate</b>.",
          "Literally: “not comforted.”",
          "The sentence fits: nothing her friends said helped."
        ],
        "a": "So sad that nothing comforts."
      },
