      {
        "t": "mistake",
        "html": "Confusing two different <i>mis</i>es. English <b>mis-</b> means wrongly (<i>mistake</i>, <i>misread</i>). But in <b>misanthrope</b>, the Greek <b>mis-</b> means <i>hate</i>: a misanthrope dislikes people in general. You will meet that part in the lesson on feeling and love. Also remember that <b>dis-</b> has three meanings: not (<i>dishonest</i>), apart (<i>dissect</i>) and away (<i>dismiss</i>)."
